<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · artifact</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cross of the Angels</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">808</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as Cruz de los Ángeles</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Cross of the Angels is a jewelled cross of gold, gems and cameos given by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-ii-of-asturias">Alfonso II of Asturias</a> to the cathedral of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oviedo">Oviedo</a> in 808. A legend says it was made by angels disguised as pilgrims. It is kept in the Cámara Santa of the cathedral, is a masterpiece of Asturian pre-Romanesque metalwork and is the emblem of the city of Oviedo.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cross-of-the-angels.jpg" alt="Cross of the Angels" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Radiostud484 · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:CrossOfTheAngels.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
